# P1-CTLR (CONTROL RE-RUN, PRODUCTION BYTES): W-0's P1a-CTL (exactness-shared) and P1b-CTL (lifecycle-evict) as ONE job on the production base image tp4-serve-10, with the cheap audit mounted over it (C2_PREFIX_KVREAD_MOUNT=1:
# the rig's opgraft-KVR/qwen_kv_read.so and opgraft-KVR/prod-audit/model.py, the production model.py staged with the narrowed audit by optimisation/ttnn-op/kv_region_read/stage_prod_audit.py; the engine is otherwise
# byte-identical to production's, and the audit's edits are inert without QWEN_PREFIX_AUDIT=1). The exactness-shared arm's first audited step is cross-checked against the whole-cache read (+~9 min, QWEN_PREFIX_AUDIT_READ=cross).
# These rows are the baselines W-2's cutover rule needs (W-0's P1a-CTL TIMEBOXed on the old audit and its P1b-CTL failed only the coverage rule, fixed on tp4/audit-cost): P1a-CTLR = the exactness-shared arm, P1b-CTLR = the lifecycle-evict arm.
# READ: both arms PASS (NO-VERDICT is not a baseline; a TIMEBOX is not retried with the same box). Needs Q1 PASS (the mount carries the same extension; a Q1 failure means P1b-CTLR-lifecycle-evict-prod-bytes instead).
# The gate refuses the exactness-shared arm before any container boots when the mounted image lacks the extension or its model.py is off this checkout's PATCHED_SHA256 (stage_prod_audit.py again after any change to qwen_prefix_model_patch).
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the region-read pack (tp4-kvread-jobs, docs/prefix-audit-cost.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the window branch and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=exactness-shared,lifecycle-evict
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_PREFIX_KVREAD_MOUNT=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=240
